| `isolation_guard` | Fails a test that reaches the network, writes outside its scratch, or opens a sqlite database or a listed live store, past its tier's rule, naming the test, the phase, the tier, the event and the fix, even when the test caught the error; a reach a test needs is a per-test exemption with a reason, and one that goes unused fails the run. Test scratch goes under one configured root, never the system temporary directory or the checkout. | automatic in every pytest run (`tests/conftest.py`) | [`tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.network`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`tests.isolation.exempt.<axis>.<test>`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`tests.isolation.stores`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`tests.scratch_root`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Defence-in-depth, not a sandbox: it judges what a Python audit event carries, so a child process, a C extension's own file or socket calls, and a name lookup are not seen. Not for a child's environment: `child_env` (`docs/adr/keel/K-0012-child-process-environment-allowlist.md`) is the sibling that holds what a spawn inherits. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
